Error [E0320]: typed collection construction uses `[T]{…}`, not `[T].{…}`
  --> tests/ui/binpat_unaligned_rest.jet:2:17
    |
  2 |     data :: [U8].{1}
    |                 ^
 Why: D-LIT-DOT1 drops the constructor dot from every literal head
 Fix: write `[T]{…}`

Error [E0320]: typed pattern construction uses `[U8]{…}`, not `[U8].{…}`
  --> tests/ui/binpat_unaligned_rest.jet:4:13
    |
  4 |         [U8].{"{a:U4}{rest:...}"} -> { print("x") }
    |             ^
 Why: D-LIT-DOT1 drops the constructor dot from every literal head
 Fix: write `[U8]{…}`

Error [E1011]: this part of the binary pattern doesn't start on a byte boundary
  --> tests/ui/binpat_unaligned_rest.jet:4:23
    |
  4 |         [U8].{"{a:U4}{rest:...}"} -> { print("x") }
    |                       ^^^^^^^^
 Why: fixed bytes and a `{rest:...}` capture are read whole-byte, so every bit-field before them must add up to a multiple of 8 bits
 Fix: pad the preceding holes to a byte boundary (e.g. add a reserved `{_:U4}`)
